  "id": "directory-code-review",
  "independence_basis": "Separate user-authorized nonauthor agent reviewed root's implementation and actual diffs; reviewer did not author or modify code, fixtures or plan. Earlier independent Design/Delivery assessment did not contribute implementation.",
  "judgment": "approved",
  "limitations": [
    "No whole-initiative completion, final Verify, CI/branch/PR readiness, cache/executor implementation, measured performance, package publication or customer adoption is claimed.",
    "Assessment concerns the actual complete directory slice and exact subjects. Existing historical drift and unrelated legacy prose debt retain their own applicability and are not erased by this review."
  ],
  "rationale": [
    "Spec alignment: pass. Exact System project layout and Design portable-default override remain on approved subjects; all twelve model locations and unique Records/Workflow example namespaces are supported. Neither user-facing skill behavior nor record JSON format changed.",
    "Test coverage: pass. New-path failure-first proof exposed eight rejected mapped paths; deleted-source/example selection also failed before repair. Current model boundary suite passes 90, selector suite passes 167 and metadata fixture suite passes 8. Unknown nested paths, example-as-model, present historical invalid files, missing paths and symlinks retain direct negative coverage.",
    "Edge cases: pass. Current examples select the precise Records owner before CLI; historical absent paths map to current owners without hiding present invalid/symlinked inputs. New map changes select both actual reader regression groups. Portable flat/matching model paths remain accepted under their existing semantics.",
    "Error handling: pass. Existing contained-regular-file, root traversal and symlink safeguards remain in validation. Shared map has no imports or execution effects; both isolated selector fixture constructors copy it. Invalid model bodies continue through the existing fail-closed structural checks rather than being waived by a recognized path.",
    "Architecture boundaries: pass. scripts/model_layout.py holds only the exact declared constant, consumed by validator and selector. It replaces the problematic full-validator import, avoiding transitive loader dependencies. Retired-method source validation resolves current Design/System owners while preserving original frozen source hashes.",
    "Compatibility: pass. Compared pre-move baseline to current mapped files: all 50 JSON/Mermaid payloads and numbered requirement rows remain exact. Prior Design assessment also established 311 preserved local link targets/anchors. Fixture-reader path updates retain original data and behavioral assertions; historical reviews/proposals/plans/archives retain original subjects rather than being silently reapproved.",
    "Security/privacy: pass. No credentials, network, release write, installation capability, new parser relaxation or record mutation path is introduced. Exact path allowlisting remains distinct from arbitrary nested acceptance; symlink and containment checks apply equally to mapped and portable paths.",
    "Derived artifact currency: pass within scope. Moved model/example source and current Markdown links are the affected artifacts; no published skill or generated package input behavior changes. Release candidate edit is a policy-path comment only. Package publication/build currency and customer adoption are not claimed.",
    "Unrelated changes: pass. Inspected executable/test diffs are bounded path mapping, selector support, moved fixture consumers and corresponding regression allocation. Full M1/M2 interaction was assessed after correction. The larger previously approved hierarchy/Validation proposal remains later implementation scope and is not declared complete.",
    "Validation evidence: pass for bounded slice. Original selector run had 23 failures and 143 passes caused by missing heavy import dependency; that failure is retained. Current full rerun passes 167. CLI initial selected run had one Workflow path failure; root fixed the fixture parent/source path and focused Workflow rerun passes both cases, with other successful selected CLI results unaffected. Metadata 8 and boundary 90 current passes corroborate direct readers. No original failing run is relabeled passed.",
    "directory-selector-dependency resolved. Independent code inspection confirms dependency-free shared map, explicit inclusion in both isolated workspaces, and direct check-selection regression for both consumers. Complete selector rerun exercises the previously failing wrapper path rather than suppressing assertions or mocking required work.",
    "Milestone handoff: both M1 relocation and M2 reader repair now have a clean independent integrated assessment. No review resolution remains for this slice. Route owns work/activity closeout; later validation executor implementation and final whole-initiative Code Review followed by distinct Verify remain mandatory. This approval cannot serve as their completed proof.",
    "Durable directory-layout-proof and directory-layout-evidence.md record the exact failure/correction/final command outcomes above. Final CLI example path-only correction was independently reassessed and directory-design-review renewed; the unchanged primary plan and directory-delivery-review remain applicable."
  ],
